**Scaling model:**
- When a second project onboards: PROJECT.md is duplicated; program-scoped governance in `pmo-platform/core/governance/` + `pmo-platform/release/governance/` and operational config in `projects/_config/` are shared.
- When a non-PMO work area onboards: Gets its own CONTEXT.md; workspace-global files are shared; `projects/_config/` files do not apply unless the work area opts in.
- Skills are workspace-global infrastructure — they live under each module's skills/ folder (`pmo-platform/core/skills/`, `pmo-platform/operations/skills/`, `pmo-platform/release/skills/`) and are deployed to all work areas via `deploy.sh`.
- Program-scoped governance files live under `pmo-platform/core/governance/` + `pmo-platform/release/governance/` (git-tracked). Program-scoped operational config lives in `projects/_config/` (Cowork-owned). No governance file should exist outside these locations (enforced by drift detection).

**Placement rule for new files:** Before creating any new governance file, check this map. If the file governs a single project → project-scoped. If it governs the program across projects → `pmo-platform/core/governance/` or `pmo-platform/release/governance/` (if git-tracked governance) or `projects/_config/` (if Cowork-owned operational config). If it applies to the whole workspace regardless of work area → workspace root. If it is a read-once analysis artifact (audit, review, gap analysis) → the operator-instance analysis path `pmo-platform/analysis/<audit-name>-YYYY-MM-DD/` (resolved per-instance) with a dated subfolder per audit. When uncertain, ask the user.

**Analysis folder convention:** Each audit or review lives in its own dated subfolder under the operator-instance analysis path `pmo-platform/analysis/` (an operator-instance workspace location, not a tracked in-repo module dir). Subfolder name format: `<audit-name>-YYYY-MM-DD/` (e.g., `tree-audit-2026-04-18/`, `skill-review-2026-04-18/`). Expected contents: a `SUMMARY.md` top-level report, optional `_templates/` / `_scores/` / `_cache/` / `evidence/` support folders, and an `issue-drafts/` folder with `NNN-kebab-name.md` files ready for `gh issue create`. This keeps multiple audits separable, dated, and reviewable.

## Platform vs. Working Content Boundary

Every file in the workspace belongs to one of two domains and one of three layers. The domain determines physical location; the layer determines management rules. This boundary drives .gitignore, release scoping, and agent routing.

### Domains

| Domain | Location | Git Status | Organizing Principle | Managing Agent |
|--------|----------|------------|---------------------|----------------|
| **Engineering** | `pmo-platform/` | Tracked | Module-oriented (core, operations, release, docs, packages) | Claude Code via git |
| **Operations** | `projects/` | Ignored | Tier-oriented (portfolio → program → project) | Cowork |

### Layers

| Layer | Git Status | Managing Agent | Contents |
|-------|------------|----------------|----------|
| **Layer 1 (Platform)** | Tracked | Claude Code via git | `CLAUDE.md`, `pmo-platform/` (entire tree), `.claude/settings.json`, `.claude/rules/` |
| **Layer 2 (Operations)** | Ignored | Cowork | `projects/` (entire tree except bridge files), `.claude/skills/` (deployment target), `.claude/settings.local.json`, `memory/` |
| **Layer 3 (Bridge)** | Ignored | Both (with rules) | See Bridge Files table below |

### Bridge Files (Layer 3)

| File | Path | Cowork Role | Claude Code Role |
|------|------|-------------|-----------------|
| PORTFOLIO.md | `projects/_config/PORTFOLIO.md` | Writes project health data | Reads for context only |

### Classification Rule

To classify any file: (1) check the Layer table above — if listed, use that layer. (2) If not listed, determine which domain folder it resides in: `pmo-platform/` → Layer 1, `projects/` → Layer 2. (3) If it resides at workspace root, check the Layer table — unlisted root files default to Layer 1.

## Routing

